   "body": "Agent : adversarial reviewer for PR #981 (Fable 5.2)\n\n**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2): APPROVE**, head 3ed988e7.\n\nThe round-1 findings are fixed:\n1. `AGENTS.md:133` names #893 and the general review, and `MAC-SESSIONS.md:103` no longer opens a `host: mac` issue for a check owed by a merge.\n2. `MAC-SESSIONS.md:68` puts `host: mac-helps` after `host: mac` in the Mac pick order.\n3. `EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md:60` and `README.md:218` cover `host: mac-helps`.\n4. The migration is recorded in the AGENTS row.\n5. The label says « deliverable measurements » (97 characters).\n\nNew findings, none blocking:\n1. **Low.** The relabel report should be on #893 and the PR body should be updated. *Author: the report is at https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/893#issuecomment-6931831052 (posted after the reviewer's search window). The body is updated.*\n2. **Detail.** `MAC-SESSIONS.md:103-104`: the section does not say whether the verify-merges session still runs a check sent to #893.\n3. **Detail.** `AGENTS.md:139`: « a follow-up of a lot (including a Mac check it owes) » still implies that Mac-check issues get opened.\n\n*Author: details 2 and 3 go to a follow-up docs issue, so that this APPROVE stays on the head.*\n\n**Verified:**\n- `python3 -m unittest discover scripts/tests`: 199 OK;\n- `tooling/docs/fold.py --check`: ok;\n- descriptions of 100 characters or fewer;\n- a repo-wide grep of `host: mac` found no contradiction.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
